.TH ZERODDS-ADMIN 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-admin \- ZeroDDS operator CLI for live domains and DDS-XML configs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-admin
.I group verb
[\fIargs\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-timeout\-ms\fR \fIT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-admin
is the operator front-end for ZeroDDS. It has two families of
sub-commands: the
.B live
groups join a running DDS domain over RTPS and report what is on the
wire, and the
.B offline
groups load a DDS-XML deployment file and analyze it without touching
the network.
.PP
Every data-bearing command accepts
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS Live (joins the domain over RTPS)
.TP
.B domain inspect \fIID\fR
Probe domain \fIID\fR and list the discovered participants, each with
its writer and reader endpoints (topic name, IDL type, RELIABLE vs
BEST_EFFORT, TRANSIENT_LOCAL vs VOLATILE), grouped by participant GUID.
.TP
.B discovery snapshot \fIID\fR
Probe domain \fIID\fR and print a raw SPDP/SEDP snapshot: the
participant list plus discovered publication / subscription counts.
.SS Offline (DDS-XML, no network)
.TP
.B config inspect \fIFILE.xml\fR
Load a DDS-XML deployment and render a domain-id-centric topology
(participants and their writers/readers grouped by resolved domain id).
.TP
.B qos validate \fIFILE.xml\fR
Check DDS-XML well-formedness and parse every library (qos / domain /
participant). Exit non-zero on a parse error.
.TP
.B qos check \fIFILE.xml\fR
Validate Request-vs-Offered (RxO) QoS compatibility of every
writer\(timesreader pair that shares a topic (DDS 1.4 \(sc2.2.3
compatibility matrix). Inline QoS and \fBqos_profile_ref\fR inheritance
are both resolved. Exit 1 if any pair is incompatible.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON instead of text.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-unknown
Offline commands: leave out what the DDS-XML 1.0 schemas do not define (the elements and
attributes of another product's file) and list each omission with its path on
standard error. Without it the first such element is an error.
.TP
.B \-\-vendor\-forms
Offline commands: read the forms other DDS products write (such as
.B <topic_filter>
as an element,
.BR qos_profile_ref ,
.BR <participant_qos> ,
IDL type names) and list each with its path on standard error. Without it the
first such form is an error that names the form DDS-XML 1.0 uses.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout\-ms " " \fIT\fR
Observation window in milliseconds for the live groups. Default: 2000.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
The base configuration file; its sibling
.IR PATH .d/
holds drop-ins. Default: the system configuration directory
.RI ( /etc/zerodds
on Linux,
.I /usr/local/etc/zerodds
on macOS).
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success / all QoS pairs compatible.
.TP
.B 1
Validation failure (incompatible QoS, parse error) or probe error.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error / bad invocation.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect a running domain and grab a JSON topology:
.PP
.RS
.nf
zerodds-admin domain inspect 0 --json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Catch incompatible QoS in a deployment before rollout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
zerodds-admin qos check deployment.xml
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-xmlc (1),
.BR zerodds-snitch (1),
.BR zerodds-spy (1),
.BR zerodds-monitor (1)
